KZ3 patch 2196 (rsx round, 2026-11-18): LD_WB_DEFER (patch 2185) is now default ON; LD_WB_DEFER=0 restores the synchronous
write-back. Measured (3 strict A/B pairs): fps_window 18.73 -> 20.60, frames over 50 ms about 320 -> 205
per run; the one bad run was a pair of whole-process pauses that also occur with the switch off.
New rsx_wbd_env_on() (unset or anything but a leading '0' = on), used by ld_wbd_mode; the SPU read-hook install in cellGcmSys.c
uses the same rule. The "ignored" notes (LD_WRITEBACK_BATCH=0, FIFO capture) only print when the switch was set explicitly.

diff --git a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
--- a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
+++ b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
@@ -5911,7 +5911,7 @@
         if (e && atoi(e) > 0 && spu_set_guest_read_hook) spu_set_guest_read_hook(gcm_spu_read_ea); }
     {   const char* e = getenv("LD_WB_READ");   /* patch 2184 */
         const char* d = getenv("LD_WB_DEFER");   /* patch 2185: the GET feed also counts reads of a pending deferred store */
-        if (((e && atoi(e) > 0) || (d && d[0] && d[0] != '0')) && spu_set_guest_read_hook2) spu_set_guest_read_hook2(gcm_spu_read_ea2); }
+        if (((e && atoi(e) > 0) || !(d && d[0] == '0')) && spu_set_guest_read_hook2) spu_set_guest_read_hook2(gcm_spu_read_ea2); }   /* 2196: unset = on */
     if (spu_set_guest_write_hook) spu_set_guest_write_hook(gcm_spu_note_pages_ea);   /* 2033; tag 2081 */
     if (fs_set_guest_write_hook) fs_set_guest_write_hook(gcm_fs_note_pages_ea);   /* patch 2078; tag 2081 */
 }
